{
  "bull_case": "The bull case rests on the significant momentum in orders which surged over fifty percent year-over-year [D1, D2, D3]. Demand for testing solutions linked to artificial intelligence infrastructure is a major contributor to this increase [D2]. The Communications Solutions Group achieved its first billion dollar quarter [D3]. Wireline revenue exceeded wireless revenue for the first time this quarter [D3]. Management expects the 6G opportunity to be larger than the 5G cycle [D3]. The company needs to see continued order strength and revenue growth at the next report [D1].",
  "bear_case": "The bear case is driven by the fact that one-time tariff impacts in fiscal 2026 will not repeat [D3]. Supply chain constraints are expected to act as a governor on near-term revenue conversion for several quarters [D3, D4]. The supply environment is currently less flexible than it was a year ago [D3]. Revenue conversion is expected to be nonlinear due to external supply dependencies [D4]. The company needs to see improved supply chain flexibility and revenue conversion at the next report [D3]."
}
